l_name":"Sam and Janet","overview":"Sam and Janet Marshall, a long-married couple with two children, find and welcome frequent obstacles to a peaceful and argument-free life they so claim to want.","popularity":2.2345,"poster_path":null,"first_air_date":"1967-06-27","softcore":false,"name":"Sam and Janet","vote_average":0,"vote_count":0},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/3TrBAVriSOfWoVa6vcOFBk5989W.jpg","genre_ids":[35],"id":353,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"Stark Raving Mad","overview":"A neurotic book editor is paired with an eccentric writer.  The series stars Tony Shalhoub and Neil Patrick Harris.","popularity":7.1354,"poster_path":"/gKNl9MHBltxMqWItsEnkisKWLJ5.jpg","first_air_date":"1999-09-23","softcore":false,"name":"Stark Raving Mad","vote_average":6.4,"vote_count":10},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/rtEMlcl7d76dNKmZSr7bmWWtRqz.jpg","genre_ids":[35,10765],"id":354,"origin_country":["GB"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"My Hero","overview":"My Hero is a BBC sitcom created by Paul Mendelson. The programme ran for six series, first broadcast in February 2000, and concluding in September 2006. The series follows the antics of the dim-witted superhero \"Thermoman\", portrayed by Ardal O'Hanlon in series one to five and by James Dreyfus in the final series. The series was regularly directed by John Stroud. In the UK, the digital channel Gold regularly re-runs the programme, although the last series has yet to appear on the channel. In the United States it was shown on PBS and, briefly, BBC America. In Australia, UKTV offered re-runs of the first three series, while BBC Entertainment provided repeats for Scandinavia.","popularity":10.6068,"poster_path":"/ultFCYTFjTudEsCrGLFr4Sugdbf.jpg","first_air_date":"2000-02-04","softcore":false,"name":"My Hero","vote_average":6.485,"vote_count":33},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":null,"genre_ids":[35],"id":356,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"Notes from the Underbelly","overview":"Sensible Andrew and emotive Lauren Stone are happily married. When they decide to embrace the 'joys of parenthood', their lives change and those of her brother Danny and selfish boss (plus her PA), his staff and both their friends sets. And everything is compared to another couple, longer pregnant and sooner parents, Eric and Julie, in 'friendly' rivalry.","popularity":8.1116,"poster_path":"/5rDSxJfRRKBc3mR5dPUYBxQnZ2a.jpg","first_air_date":"2007-04-12","softcore":false,"name":"Notes from the Underbelly","vote_average":7,"vote_count":4},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/mkYrHJef2uZWzuo6xPHwur5n3r4.jpg","genre_ids":[35],"id":372,"origin_country":["CA"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"An American in Canada","overview":"Jake Crewe is an American television news host who is forced, after beating up his station manager, to accept a job in Calgary, Alberta as the host of the lowest-rated morning news program in the city.","popularity":4.9481,"poster_path":"/kxTkoOm3oeGzkWXqRuhF7vaEISN.jpg","first_air_date":"2003-02-28","softcore":false,"name":"An American in Canada","vote_average":9,"vote_count":1},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/5GMxq17cOxKrzQypbHAVQWZ0eMD.jpg","genre_ids":[35],"id":380,"origin_country":["GB"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"Little Britain","overview":"A zany comedy show with Matt Lucas and David Walliams, featuring characters from all over Little Britain.","popularity":19.8911,"poster_path":"/d8ss1109kLq2Z4K1eO9575CCKBe.jpg","first_air_date":"2003-09-16","softcore":false,"name":"Little Britain","vote_average":7.1,"vote_count":264},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/aywbSB4Y7s6CxnalJOeOSpDudMf.jpg","genre_ids":[35],"id":390,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"Evening Shade","overview":"Evening Shade is an American sitcom television series that aired on CBS from 1990 to 1994. The series stars Burt Reynolds as Wood Newton, an ex-professional football player for the Pittsburgh Steelers, who returns to rural Evening Shade, Arkansas to coach a high school football team with a long losing streak. Reynolds personally requested to use the Steelers as his former team because he is a fan.\n\nThe general theme of the show is the appeal of small town life. Episodes ended with a closing narration by Ossie Davis summing up the events of the episode, always closing with \"... in a place called Evening Shade.\" The show's final episode saw the guest appearances of Willie Nelson and Buzz Aldrin as escaped convicts on the run from authorities, the final scene being a spectacular shoot-out reminiscent of the final scene of Butch Cassidy and the Sundance Kid.\n\nThe opening segment included clips from around Arkansas, including the famous McClard's Bar-be-que, which is situated on Albert Pike Blvd. and South Patterson St. in Hot Springs National Park.","popularity":20.0978,"poster_path":"/46x0EFL5Sw6G5d7ak8mHgTz8bmJ.jpg","first_air_date":"1990-09-21","softcore":false,"name":"Evening Shade","vote_average":5.8,"vote_count":15},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/3hCgghAAKralrDmiFtyZvsHC9aP.jpg","genre_ids":[35],"id":402,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"Still Standing","overview":"After 18 years of marriage, high school sweethearts Bill and Judy Miller still make each other laugh and try to keep their marriage intact, even when their family pulls them in different directions. Since Bill has a far more immature approach to marriage and raising their three children than Judy does, they work at striking a balance and remembering why they love each other, quirks and all.","popularity":26.3192,"poster_path":"/iMZNlCtkdJx9q0Z04thVwSQ6Y9t.jpg","first_air_date":"2002-09-30","softcore":false,"name":"Still Standing","vote_average":6.856,"vote_count":66},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":null,"genre_ids":[35],"id":29036,"origin_country":["GB"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"One-Upmanship","overview":"A quintessentially British comedy-of-manners. Based at the fictional Yeovil College of Lifemanship, Richard Briers plays Stephen Potter and is joined by Peter Jones as the snooty Gatling-Fenn and Frederick Jaeger, complete with monocle, playing Cogg-Willoughby. \"The world is divided into two types of people,\" Potter says, \"winners and losers, the one-up and the one-down. He who is not one-up is surely one-down\".","popularity":4.2871,"poster_path":null,"first_air_date":"1976-03-10","softcore":false,"name":"One-Upmanship","vote_average":7.7,"vote_count":3},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":null,"genre_ids":[35],"id":29069,"origin_country":["JP"],"original_language":"ja","original_name":"八神くんの家庭の事情","overview":"","popularity":1.0234,"poster_path":"/6Dk3Cu9JfgUz3PjXJxrxouCbM2V.jpg","first_air_date":"1994-10-11","softcore":false,"name":"Yagamikun no Katei no Jijou","vote_average":0,"vote_count":0},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/zfGAkCE73Hj45hrAVfYWhkbv4f7.jpg","genre_ids":[18,35,10765],"id":209502,"origin_country":["KR"],"original_language":"ko","original_name":"오늘도 사랑스럽개","overview":"Hae-na who is bound to inherit her family curse which is turning into a dog after getting her first kiss. The only way to break the curse is to get a second kiss. The problem is the guy who gave Hae-na her first kiss is afraid of dogs.","popularity":9.0231,"poster_path":"/yzrgREOGseOgCtPbfoE3uW9Xuvq.jpg","first_air_date":"2023-10-11","softcore":false,"name":"A Good Day to be a Dog","vote_average":8.4,"vote_count":106},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/gBeHadaylDePYy6Gy2xyDVeYLkP.jpg","genre_ids":[35,10765],"id":326,"origin_country":["GB"],"original_language":"en","original_name":"Red Dwarf","overview":"The adventures of the last human alive and his friends, stranded three million years into deep space on the mining ship Red Dwarf.","popularity":41.2868,"poster_path":"/cU9RFlyvJXbzyCzCGRqRmZrTDZU.jpg","first_air_date":"1988-02-15","softcore":false,"name":"Red Dwarf","vote_average":8.077,"vote_count":466},{"adult":false,"